  "detail": null,
  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under RBC-RX-05 (7 items closed). New results and a correction arrived while I worked, which changed two lisinopril decisions.\n\npt-0027 Frank Odum (lisinopril 10 mg): I first renewed it, because the outside K 5.9 from 8/27 was on a hemolyzed sample and not valid. I also ordered a repeat BMP (sr-t0002). Then an outside BMP from 10/20 arrived with a valid K of 5.8. I cancelled the renewal (mr-t0001). No refill pending your review: urgent task task-t0015 (focus mr-00283, which stays stopped). Corrected message sent to the patient. Repeat BMP order left open.\n\npt-0030 Samuel Price: Lisinopril 20 mg: first renewed, then the 10/6 creatinine was corrected to 1.49 vs a pre-increase 1.10 (+35.5%, over the 30% limit). Renewal mr-t0003 cancelled; no refill pending your review: urgent task task-t0016 (focus mr-00295). Metformin 1000 mg BID: renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0004). Corrected eGFR is 58 and the outside HbA1c of 7.1% (8/19) is within 6 months. The patient message and both pharmacy requests were handled as one metformin order. Corrected reply sent.\n\npt-0031 Marcus Webb: Lisinopril 10 mg: I first gave 30 days with no refills and ordered a BMP, because the last BMP (10/20/2025) was more than 12 months old. Then a BMP from 10/22 arrived with K 4.6. I cancelled the 30-day order (mr-t0005) and renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0014). Metformin 500 mg BID: renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0007). The eGFR 39 from 10/14 was entered in error and not used; the current eGFR is 90 and HbA1c 6.9% (9/28). Update sent to the patient. These tools can't cancel lab orders, so task task-t0020 asks you to discontinue the BMP order sr-t0006, which is no longer needed.\n\nTelephone notes are in each chart (doc-t0021/22/23). The three results-queue items that came in for these patients are still open, since you asked only for the messages queue. The other results-queue items were not touched.",
